        "matched_product": "loose leaf green tea",
        "snippet": "Buy loose leaf green tea online — Chinese green teas, Japanese green teas, and flavored green blends. Sencha, Gunpowder, Jasmine, matcha, and more. From 15¢/cup. Christmas Gifts tea samplers horoscope gifts flavor trilogy tea starter sets gift cards loose tea gifts teabag gifts tea candles portions wedding favors custom gift box mystery box literary sampler ... Shop online for loose leaf green teas made from whole tea leaves sourced directly from the artisan farmers who tend them. Japan's most widely consumed tea and the reference point for what Japanese green tea tastes like. Adagio's loose leaf Sencha is steamed in the traditional Japanese style - clean, fresh, with a natural sweetness and a gentle umami depth that distinguishes quality Sencha from the flat, bitter versions that give green tea its undeserved reputation for difficulty. What makes it green rather than black or oolong is the processing: immediately after harvest, the fresh leaves are heated - either pan-fired in a wok (the Chinese method) or steamed (the Japanese method) - to stop oxidation before it begins. The result is a tea that retains the fresh, green character of the leaf rather than developing the darker, more oxidized flavors of black tea. China's most celebrated green tea - Long Jing (龍井), or Dragon Well - from the hills above West Lake in Hangzhou, Zhejiang province. Pan-fired in a flat-leaf style that produces the characteristic chestnut and fresh grass notes of authentic Long Jing, Dragon Well is the green tea that most clearly illustrates the difference between Chinese and Japanese green tea processing.",
